<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Marx</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Marx was a German philosopher, political theorist and revolutionary socialist whose theory of historical materialism analysed social change through class struggle and predicted that communism would replace capitalism. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>, he co-wrote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-communist-manifesto">The Communist Manifesto</a> with Friedrich Engels; it was first published in February 1848. Expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> after the revolutions of that year, he settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, where he wrote Das Kapital, whose first volume was published in 1867. Elected to the General Council of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-workingmens-association">First International</a> at its founding in 1864, he opposed the anarchists led by Mikhail Bakunin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-marx.jpg" alt="Karl Marx" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Jabez Edwin Mayall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_Marx_001_restored.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
